                    "text": "param dry_wet_mix 1 @min 0 @max 1",
                    "varname": "dry_wet_mix"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-36",
                    "linecount": 67,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 577.0, 986.0 ],
                    "text": "================================================================================\nchorus_leslie_doppler_sdf — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nOVERVIEW\nA standalone stereo Rotary Leslie Cabinet Chorus uniting three DAFx papers:\n1. Julius O. Smith, Stefania Serafin, Jonathan Abel, and David Berners (DAFx-02: \"Doppler Simulation and the Leslie\", Sections 3.2 & 4.1, Eq. 10–20) + Sascha Disch and Udo Zölzer (DAFx-99 Section 4, Fig. 8–9): Simulates the 180-degree opposite dual horns with circular Doppler delay modulation (~0.5 ms excursion), synchronous directional radiation amplitude modulation, tube amplifier soft overdrive (\"growl\"), and wooden cabinet cross-reflections.\n2. Jussi Pekonen, Tapani Pihlajamäki, and Vesa Välimäki (DAFx-11 Paper 49, Sections 3.1 & 3.2, Eq. 1–5, Fig. 2, Table 1): Splits the signal at an 800 Hz crossover into Treble Horn and Bass Drum pathways, applying the exact Table 1 time-varying Spectral Delay Filter (SDF) allpass cascades (Treble: N = 4 stages, Mb = -0.75, Ms = 0.20; Bass: N = 3 stages, Mb = -0.92, Ms = 0.04) with decoupled physical motor acceleration inertia and 0.1–0.3 Hz treble/bass motor mistuning!\n\nINLETS & OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: Stereo Audio Input (Tuba; mono in1 auto-normalizes to stereo)\n- in3: Optional Chorale/Tremolo Speed Throw Input [0..1] (patch a footswitch, gate, or envelope to ramp the horn and drum motors up to Tremolo with realistic mechanical inertia!)\n- in4: Unused / Thru\n- out1 / out2: Stereo Rotary Leslie Cabinet Output\n\nPARAMETERS (7)\n\n1. speed_chorale_tremolo\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (0.0 = Slow Chorale ~0.8 Hz, 1.0 = Fast Tremolo ~6.2 Hz; Default: 0.25)\n   - Taper: Linear speed control with decoupled physical motor inertia slews (the light treble horn accelerates 3x faster than the heavy wooden bass drum, DAFx-11 Section 3.2).\n   - Function: Controls the rotational speed of the dual-motor Leslie cabinet.\n\n2. doppler_horn_depth\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (maps to 0.0 to 0.55 ms Circular Horn Doppler Delay Excursion, Default: 0.65)\n   - Taper: Linear Doppler radius scaling (DAFx-99 Section 4, DAFx-02 Eq. 20).\n   - Function: Controls the true time-domain Doppler pitch shift of the two 180-degree opposing treble horns above 800 Hz.\n\n3. sdf_dispersion_depth\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (Spectral Delay Filter Allpass Dispersion Depth, Default: 0.70)\n   - Taper: Linear scaler on Table 1 modulator depths Ms (DAFx-11 Eq. 5).\n   - Function: Modulates the 4-stage Treble SDF around bias Mb = -0.75 and the 3-stage Bass SDF around bias Mb = -0.92, adding rich frequency-dependent phase chorus to both the sub-800 Hz tuba fundamental and upper harmonics.\n\n4. directional_am_depth\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (Synchronous Horn/Drum Directional Radiation AM, Default: 0.55)\n   - Taper: Linear AM depth (DAFx-99 Fig. 8, DAFx-11 Section 3.2).\n   - Function: Synchronizes amplitude maxima with the stationary zero-Doppler points as the horn mouth sweeps past each virtual stereo microphone.\n\n5. tube_amp_growl_db\n   - Range: 0.0 to 18.0 dB (Leslie Tube Amplifier Overdrive \"Growl\", Default: 4.5 dB)\n   - Taper: Logarithmic dB-to-linear gain into level-compensated tanh saturation before the 800 Hz crossover (DAFx-02 Section 1).\n   - Function: Adds warm tube harmonic growl before the rotating crossover.\n\n6. cabinet_stereo_width\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (Stereo Microphone Separation vs. 0.7 Cabinet Cross-Reflection, Default: 0.80)\n   - Taper: Linear stereo width (DAFx-99 Fig. 9).\n   - Function: Blends between the natural 0.7 acoustic cross-bleed inside the wooden cabinet and wide stereo isolation of the two opposing horns/rotors.\n\n7. dry_wet_mix\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (0% Dry to 100% Rotary Cabinet; Default: 1.00)\n   - Taper: Linear crossfade.\n   - Function: Blends dry tuba with the full stereo Leslie cabinet.\n",
                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                }
            }
        ],
